//! Byte-level snapshots of everything jails generates.
//!
//! This target exists to make refactoring the generators *safe*. The Java
//! templates are being moved out of Rust `format!` strings and into
//! `templates/`, which is a large mechanical change to code that works, and
//! the only acceptable evidence that such a change is behaviour-preserving is
//! that every generated byte is identical before and after.
//!
//! It is deliberately end-to-end rather than one snapshot per template
//! function: ~20 invocations cover all 80-odd template functions
//! transitively, through the same path a user takes, and a template that is
//! rendered with the wrong arguments is caught as well as one whose text
//! changed.
//!
//! ## Updating
//!
//! ```text
//! UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test --test golden
//! ```
//!
//! Then **read the diff**. That is the whole point: a change to generated
//! output should be visible and deliberate. `git diff tests/golden` is the
//! review. Regenerating without reading is how a snapshot suite stops being
//! an oracle and starts being a rubber stamp -- which is why the assertions
//! below also check a few semantic properties that a blind regeneration
//! would not fix.

mod common;

use common::*;
use std::collections::BTreeMap;
use std::fs;
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

/// Which fixture a scenario starts from.
#[derive(Copy, Clone)]
enum Fixture {
    Plain,
    Spring,
}

struct Scenario {
    /// Directory under `tests/golden/`.
    name: &'static str,
    fixture: Fixture,
    /// jails invocations, run in order.
    steps: &'static [&'static [&'static str]],
}

